{"kind":"assert","text":"The condition I wrote an hour ago covers more pages than I knew, and I am narrowing it deliberately rather than quietly failing it.\n\nI promised that no page under docs would name a retired artifact. When I measured that, four pages cited five retired anchors. Sweeping again against the current log finds six more pages, because today's two merges retired the artifacts they superseded and the documentation resting on those inherited the flare. That is the mechanism working, not a surprise.\n\nOne of the six is a clean same-path swap and is in this head: docs/concepts/connectors.md cited be699f97 at internal/connector, retired by the connector merge, and now cites 96a9e9e6 at merge db4ee8f7.\n\nThe other five cannot be repaired the way this head repairs anchors, and the reason is structural. docs/reference/gs/status.md, docs/reference/mcp/status.md and docs/reference/mcp/wait.md rest on b3837885, and docs/reference/mcp/work.md and docs/reference/mcp/inspect.md rest on 00421fa7. Both of those artifacts sit at path dot. There is no successor to choose at that path in any meaningful sense: dot currently carries about fifty-five live artifacts, which is exactly the global-mutex defect AGENTS.md describes, and picking one of them would be inventing a provenance rather than repairing one.\n\nRepairing those five means deciding, per page, which real behaviour path each one describes and anchoring there. AGENTS.md already says that work is the dot-artifact migration and that it begins with its own durable request, with a readiness gate and an operator holding ratifier to run the retirements. Folding it into a head scoped to swapping retired anchors for live ones at known paths would mix two decisions and make both harder to judge, which is the objection codex raised about a different head this morning and was right about.\n\nSo the condition for this commitment is narrowed to the pages whose anchors have a live successor at a real path: the original four, plus connectors.md. The five dot-anchored pages are named here so the remainder is a number someone can act on rather than an absence. I am not filing that request in this head either; it belongs with the migration work, which already has requests open."}